<title>USA: NYC official sees vote on new authority on Feb 26.</title>
<headline>NYC official sees vote on new authority on Feb 26.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York City's budget director on Thursday said he expected the state Senate and Assembly to vote on Feb 26 on a new financing arm for the city that would let it borrow up to $7.5 billion of debt.</p>
<p>Joseph Lhota, saying lawmakers had reached agreement on the new New York City Transitional Finance Authority, said, &quot;The governor should sign it shortly thereafter.&quot;</p>
<p>Lhota was speaking at a board meeting of the Municipal Assistance Corporation for the City of New York.</p>
<p>((--Joan Gralla, 212-859-1654))</p>
